<section class="section">
  <div class="container container--narrow center">
    <span class="eyebrow">Order <%= order.reference %></span>
    <h1 class="mt-1">Confirming your payment</h1>
    <p class="lede mt-2" style="margin-inline:auto">
      Stripe hasn't confirmed this one yet. That's normal for some payment methods and usually
      resolves within a minute — we're waiting on the webhook rather than guessing.
    </p>
    <div class="row mt-4" style="justify-content:center">
      <a class="btn btn--accent" href="/checkout/complete?ref=<%= order.reference %>">Check again</a>
      <a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/account">Go to my account</a>
    </div>
    <p class="tiny muted mt-3">
      Nothing is lost either way — once the payment confirms, the templates appear in the account for
      <b><%= order.email %></b>. Email <a href="mailto:<%= store.supportEmail %>"><%= store.supportEmail %></a> with the order reference if it's still pending in an hour.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
